{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What types of books can be printed (paperback, hardcover, spiral-bound)?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "We print across all major binding formats, perfect-bound paperbacks, case-bound hardcovers with dust jackets or case laminate, spiral-bound and wire-bound books, saddle-stitched booklets, and coil-bound workbooks. The right binding depends on your book's purpose, page count, and how it'll be used. Novels and narrative non-fiction typically suit perfect-bound paperback or hardcover. Workbooks, cookbooks, and reference guides often benefit from spiral or wire binding that lets pages lie flat. We'll recommend the best option for your specific book during your consultation."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you offer both short-run and bulk book printing services?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Short-run printing covers anything from a single proof copy to a few hundred units, ideal for author copies, local events, limited editions, or testing demand before committing to larger quantities. Bulk printing starts at around 500 copies and uses offset production methods that significantly reduce per-unit cost at higher volumes. We also offer print-on-demand, which eliminates minimum quantities entirely by printing each copy individually as orders come in. The right approach depends on your sales strategy, your budget, and whether you need physical inventory or prefer zero-stock distribution."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What file format is required for printing my book?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Print-ready PDF is the standard file format for book printing. Your interior PDF needs to include correct trim marks, bleed settings, embedded fonts, and appropriate resolution for all images (300 DPI minimum). Your cover file needs to be a single PDF incorporating front cover, spine, and back cover at the correct dimensions for your page count and trim size. If you don't have print-ready files, we offer formatting and cover design services that produce files built to the exact specifications of your chosen printing method, so you don't need to learn pre-press production to get your book printed."
      }
