      "name": "What is a book trailer video and how does it work?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A book trailer video is a short promotional video, typically thirty seconds to two minutes, designed to generate interest in your book the same way a film trailer generates interest in a movie. It uses visuals, music, text, and sometimes voice-over to create atmosphere and curiosity around your book without giving away the full story. Book trailers are shared on YouTube, social media, author websites, and Amazon author pages, giving potential readers a visual, emotional introduction to your book that a cover image and blurb can't replicate."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you create cinematic or animated book trailers?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Both. We produce cinematic trailers using live-action footage, professional colour grading, and atmospheric sound design, as well as animated trailers using motion graphics, illustrated sequences, and typographic animation. The right style depends on your genre, your budget, and where the trailer will be used. Some books suit cinematic treatment, others work better with animation, and many benefit from a combination. We'll recommend the best approach during your consultation based on your specific book and goals."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does it take to produce a book trailer video?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Standard production takes two to four weeks from creative brief to final delivery, depending on the complexity of the trailer and the style of production involved. Animated trailers and cinematic trailers with custom footage typically sit at the longer end. Simpler typographic or text-based trailers can be completed faster. Rush production is available for urgent launch deadlines, subject to availability. We'll give you a clear timeline during your consultation and keep you updated throughout production."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What materials do I need to provide for a trailer?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "At minimum, we need your book's cover image, a synopsis or blurb, and any specific vision you have for the trailer's tone and feel. Beyond that, the more you can share the better, key quotes from the book, comparable titles whose marketing you admire, details about your target audience, and any existing brand assets like logos or author photos. If you don't have all of this ready, that's fine. Part of our process is helping you define the creative direction during the briefing stage."
