        "text": "eBook writing services in Melbourne are professional writing services where an experienced writer produces a complete eBook manuscript on your behalf, fiction, non-fiction, business guides, self-help, how-to content, or any other category, based on your ideas, expertise, and vision. You provide the concept and direction. The writer provides the structure, research where needed, and the words. The finished manuscript belongs entirely to you, with your name as the author and full ownership of all rights. At Melbourne Print and Publish, we offer eBook writing services across every category for authors and professionals in Melbourne and across Australia."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does the eBook writing process work in Melbourne?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It starts with a detailed briefing, a conversation about your eBook concept, your target audience, your goals, and what you want the finished book to accomplish. Your writer then develops a full chapter outline for your approval before writing begins. The manuscript is written in stages, with drafts shared in batches so you can give feedback and request changes before we move forward. Nothing is finalised without your approval at every stage. The whole process is genuinely collaborative, you’re shaping the eBook as it develops, not waiting months to see a finished draft you’ve had no input on."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much do eBook writing services cost in Melbourne?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "eBook writing costs in Melbourne vary depending on the length, category, and complexity of the project. A shorter business eBook based on existing material costs less than a full-length fiction manuscript or a research-heavy instructional guide. Most professional eBook writing services charge per word or per project, with rates reflecting the writer’s experience and the scope of work involved. We don’t publish fixed rates because they rarely reflect what a specific project actually needs. Get in touch with your concept and we’ll give you a clear, honest quote built around your eBook specifically."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does it take to write an eBook in Melbourne?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
