{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is a fiction ghostwriting service in Melbourne?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A fiction ghostwriting service is a professional writing service where an experienced ghostwriter produces a fiction manuscript on your behalf, a novel, novella, or short fiction collection, based on your ideas, characters, and story concept. You provide the vision and direction. The ghostwriter provides the craft and the words. The finished manuscript belongs entirely to you, with your name as the author and full ownership of all rights. At Melbourne Print and Publish, we offer fiction ghostwriting across every genre for authors in Melbourne and across Australia, matching each project with a writer who specialises in that specific category."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does fiction ghostwriting work in Melbourne?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It starts with a detailed briefing, a conversation about your story concept, characters, genre, tone, and what you want the finished novel to feel like. Your ghostwriter then develops a full chapter outline for your approval before writing begins. The manuscript is written in stages, with drafts shared in batches so you can give feedback before we move forward. Nothing is finalised without your approval at every stage. The whole process is genuinely collaborative rather than something that happens to your story without your involvement."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does fiction ghostwriting cost in Melbourne?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Fiction ghostwriting costs vary depending on the length of your novel, the genre, and the complexity of the work involved. A shorter contemporary novel costs less than a long, complex fantasy manuscript with extensive world-building. Most professional ghostwriters charge either per word or per project, with rates reflecting experience and the scope of what’s involved. We don’t publish fixed rates because they rarely reflect what a specific project costs. Get in touch with your story concept and we’ll give you a clear, honest quote built around your book specifically."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does it take to ghostwrite a fiction book in Melbourne?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A standard fiction manuscript of around 70,000 to 80,000 words typically takes three to six months from briefing to final delivery, accounting for outlining, chapter drafting, and revision rounds. Shorter novellas take considerably less time. Longer or more complex manuscripts, multi-book series, heavily researched historical fiction, detailed fantasy world-building, take longer. We’ll give you a realistic timeline at the start of your project based on your specific manuscript and publication goals, and we communicate promptly if anything changes along the way."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I own the rights to my book after hiring a fiction ghostwriter?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, completely and from day one. Everything produced belongs entirely to you, the manuscript, the content, and the finished book, including publishing rights, adaptation rights, and all future royalties. Our ghostwriters work under a confidentiality agreement and have no claim over the work they produce for you. Your name goes on the cover, and the book is yours in every legal and creative sense. We don’t retain any rights, credit, or ongoing interest in the work after delivery."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can a ghostwriter turn my idea into a full fiction novel?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Absolutely, and that’s exactly what fiction ghostwriting is built for. You don’t need a complete outline or detailed plot structure before getting in touch. Some clients come with fully developed concepts, detailed character profiles, and chapter-by-chapter notes. Others come with nothing more than a premise and a genre. We work with both, using the briefing and outlining process to develop the story into something complete and well-structured before writing begins. If you have an idea worth turning into a novel, we can help you get it there."
      }
    }
  ]
}

{
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
